## Problem solving process analysis

Lewis earns ${weekly_earnings} every week during {num_weeks} weeks of harvest.
He has to pay ${weekly_rent} rent every week.

Total earnings = {total_earnings} = {weekly_earnings} × {num_weeks}
Total rent paid = {total_rent} = {weekly_rent} × {num_weeks}
Money remaining at end = {remaining_money} = {total_earnings} - {total_rent}

The answer is {remaining_money} = {total_earnings} - {total_rent}

## Actual analysis and solution process

In this question, {weekly_earnings} = 491, {num_weeks} = 1181, and {weekly_rent} = 216.

Total earnings = 491 × 1181 = 579,871
Total rent = 216 × 1181 = 255,096
Remaining money = 579,871 - 255,096 = 324,775

The answer is 324775
